From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] media: rockchip: vpu981: bound the AV1 tile counts before
 they index arrays

tile_cols and tile_rows arrive from userspace in the AV1 frame control as u8
and reach fixed-size arrays and a fixed scratch buffer without ever being
range-checked.

rockchip_vpu981_av1_dec_set_tile_info() divides context_update_tile_id by
tile_cols, so a zero count is a divide error. It then indexes
tile_info->width_in_sbs_minus_1[] and height_in_sbs_minus_1[] -- each
V4L2_AV1_MAX_TILE_COLS / V4L2_AV1_MAX_TILE_ROWS (64) entries -- by the column
and row counts, writes tile_cols * tile_rows sixteen-byte records into the
tile_info scratch buffer (sized for AV1_MAX_TILES records), and indexes the
tile_group_entry control (V4L2_AV1_MAX_TILE_COUNT entries) by
tile1 * tile_cols + tile0. rockchip_vpu981_av1_dec_tiles_reallocate() sizes its
per-column DMA buffers as a multiple of tile_cols. A count of 255 in either
dimension therefore overflows the scratch buffer, reads the sbs arrays and the
tile-group control out of bounds, and can divide by zero, all before the
hardware is programmed.

The V4L2 core does not catch this: validate_av1_frame() checks quantization,
segmentation, loop filter, cdef, loop restoration, the frame flags and
superres_denom, but never the tile counts.

Reject an out-of-range count in prepare_run, so the buffer is failed with
VB2_BUF_STATE_ERROR instead of the decoder corrupting memory. The per-dimension
bounds are the uAPI array sizes, which are also the AV1 maxima, so no conforming
stream is refused by them. The product is capped at AV1_MAX_TILES, the size of
the tile_info scratch this core fills; a frame with more tiles cannot be decoded
by this hardware regardless.

/dev/videoN is group video, so this is reachable by any local user in that
group, and by anything that feeds the decoder controls parsed from an untrusted
bitstream.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../verisilicon/rockchip_vpu981_hw_av1_dec.c  | 38 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 38 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/rockchip_vpu981_hw_av1_dec.c b/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/rockchip_vpu981_hw_av1_dec.c
index e4e21ad37..74601ac09 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/rockchip_vpu981_hw_av1_dec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/verisilicon/rockchip_vpu981_hw_av1_dec.c
@@ -427,6 +427,41 @@ int rockchip_vpu981_av1_dec_init(struct hantro_ctx *ctx)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * tile_cols and tile_rows arrive from userspace in the AV1 frame control as u8
+ * and reach fixed-size arrays and a fixed scratch buffer with no range check:
+ * validate_av1_frame() in the V4L2 core never looks at them.
+ *
+ * set_tile_info() divides by tile_cols (a zero count is a divide error), indexes
+ * tile_info->width_in_sbs_minus_1[] / height_in_sbs_minus_1[] -- each
+ * V4L2_AV1_MAX_TILE_COLS / _ROWS entries -- by the column and row counts, writes
+ * tile_cols * tile_rows sixteen-byte records into tile_info.cpu (AV1_MAX_TILES
+ * records), and indexes the tile_group_entry control (V4L2_AV1_MAX_TILE_COUNT
+ * entries) by tile1 * tile_cols + tile0. tiles_reallocate() sizes its per-column
+ * buffers as a multiple of tile_cols. All of that runs before the hardware is
+ * touched, so an out-of-range count corrupts memory rather than failing a decode.
+ *
+ * Bound every count here. The per-dimension limits are the uAPI array sizes,
+ * which are also the AV1 maxima, so no conforming stream is refused by them. The
+ * product is capped at AV1_MAX_TILES: that is the size of the tile_info scratch
+ * this core fills, so a frame with more tiles cannot be decoded by this hardware
+ * regardless -- refuse it cleanly instead of overflowing the buffer.
+ */
+static int rockchip_vpu981_av1_dec_validate_tile_info(struct hantro_ctx *ctx)
+{
+	const struct v4l2_av1_tile_info *tile_info =
+		&ctx->av1_dec.ctrls.frame->tile_info;
+
+	if (tile_info->tile_cols < 1 ||
+	    tile_info->tile_cols > V4L2_AV1_MAX_TILE_COLS ||
+	    tile_info->tile_rows < 1 ||
+	    tile_info->tile_rows > V4L2_AV1_MAX_TILE_ROWS ||
+	    tile_info->tile_cols * tile_info->tile_rows > AV1_MAX_TILES)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int rockchip_vpu981_av1_dec_prepare_run(struct hantro_ctx *ctx)
 {
 	struct hantro_av1_dec_hw_ctx *av1_dec = &ctx->av1_dec;
@@ -448,6 +483,9 @@ static int rockchip_vpu981_av1_dec_prepare_run(struct hantro_ctx *ctx)
 	ctrls->film_grain =
 	    hantro_get_ctrl(ctx, V4L2_CID_STATELESS_AV1_FILM_GRAIN);
 
+	if (rockchip_vpu981_av1_dec_validate_tile_info(ctx))
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	return rockchip_vpu981_av1_dec_tiles_reallocate(ctx);
 }
 
